        A supplement bought voluntarily, taken for a benefit that arrives at week 12, does worse.
        Format matters because format is what determines whether the bottle is empty at the end of
        the month or still two-thirds full.
      </p>

      <h2 id="compare">How do collagen tablets, sachets and shots compare?</h2>

      <p>
        On dose delivered per serving, the ranking is shots and sachets first, gummies and tablets
        last. On convenience the order flips for sachets, which need water, a spoon and thirty
        seconds you may not give them. Cost per gram runs in the opposite direction to convenience
        almost perfectly.
      </p>

